course: dictionary
lesson: 5203
title: Jambon, the French word for ham
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Jambon is a French word, not an English one. It means ham. You will see it on French menus and in French cafés, and you will hear it when someone orders a sandwich. Say it like zhom-BON, with the end sound pushed through your nose.
explain: Jambon often joins other words. «Un sandwich au jambon» means a sandwich with ham in it. The little word au means with, so au jambon means with ham.
explain: Look at «un jambon-beurre is a baguette with ham and butter, one of the most popular sandwiches in France.» The clues are ham, butter and baguette. A jambon-beurre is a ham and butter sandwich on a long French bread, so jambon must mean ham.
fact: Jambon means ham in French.
fact: Jambon is not an English word, so you will only see it in French texts, menus and conversations.
fact: «Un jambon-beurre» means a baguette with ham and butter.
fact: «Un sandwich au jambon» means a sandwich with ham.
fact: Jambon is a noun, and in French it is written with le before it: le jambon means the ham.
exercise: What does jambon mean in English? | Butter | *Ham | Cheese | Bread
exercise: Which two ingredients are in a jambon-beurre? | Cheese and tomato | Egg and lettuce | *Ham and butter | Jam and butter
exercise: Ella sees «un sandwich au jambon» on a café menu. What should she expect? | A sandwich with fish | *A sandwich with ham | Cheese and onion | A sandwich with jam
test: Is jambon an English word? | Yes, it is a kind of butter | Yes, it is an English word for a type of bread | Yes, it means cheese | *No, it is French for ham
test: How does jambon sound to an English ear? | JAM-bon, like the spread | *zhom-BON, with a nasal ending | JAM-bun, like a bread roll | zhoo-BAHN, long and sharp
exam: What is a jambon-beurre? | *A baguette with ham and butter | A bowl of soup | A glass of milk | A cake with jam
